# The table scene: column headers + click-to-sort on the For
# vocabulary (docs/tables-plan.md). column#0 is the For container (the
# root is a row, the reorder scene's rule). expect_columns reads the
# header bar AS THE TABLE PATH PRESENTED IT — size class, titles in
# visual order, the indicator as ^N (asc) or vN (desc); expect_rows
# reads per-row cell labels in the toolkit's child order, rows joined
# with `|`, cells with `,` — the two-level expect_order, because a
# creation-order registry cannot see the moves a sort makes. A header
# click is a REQUEST: the platform sorts nothing; the guest reorders
# by key and re-declares the indicator, so every expectation below is
# the guest's policy (same column flips, a new column starts
# ascending) coming back through the toolkit.
expect_columns column#0 "regular/Name|Size"
expect_rows column#0 "banana,30|apple,10|cherry,20"
header_click column#0 0
expect_columns column#0 "regular/Name|Size ^0"
expect_rows column#0 "apple,10|banana,30|cherry,20"
header_click column#0 0
expect_columns column#0 "regular/Name|Size v0"
expect_rows column#0 "cherry,20|banana,30|apple,10"
header_click column#0 1
expect_columns column#0 "regular/Name|Size ^1"
expect_rows column#0 "apple,10|cherry,20|banana,30"
